011health failure.    **Failure\u2011Probability\u00a0Estimate**   - HPT\u2011related failure probability in the next\u202f20\u201130\u202fcycles \u2248\u202f78\u202f% (high\u2011risk).   - Overall engine\u2011wide failure probability \u2248\u202f45\u202f% (driven mainly by the HPT condition).    **Recommended\u00a0Maintenance\u00a0Strategy**    | Horizon | Action | Reason | |---------|--------|--------| | **Immediate (\u2264\u202f1\u20112\u202fflights)** | \u2022 Ground\u2011stop for a detailed HPT inspection (borescope, vibration, thermography).<br>\u2022 Verify HPT coolant\u2011bleed valve operation and sensor calibration.<br>\u2022 Review throttle\u2011resolver data for control\u2011system anomalies. | Confirms the source of the temperature/efficiency anomaly and prevents catastrophic failure. | | **Short\u2011Term (next\u202f5\u201110\u202fcycles)** | \u2022 If fouling/tip\u2011clearance growth is found, clean or replace affected HPT blades.<br>\u2022 Re\u2011calibrate HPT temperature and efficiency sensors.<br>\u2022 Conduct a short\u2011duration engine test after maintenance to validate restored performance. | Restores HPT efficiency and stabilises temperature trends. |", "observation": "Task finished successfully"}
